{
  "description": "How fast the archive is draining and how much is left -- the figures phaze-zaf2l had to obtain by hand-querying Postgres.",
  "editable": true,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Throughput",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Audio-seconds admitted per wall-second, which is the same number as audio-hours per wall-hour. phaze-zaf2l measured 2.7183 across 410 completions over 7 days by joining analysis_completed_at to metadata.duration in psql. This is that figure, live.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 4,
          "unit": ""
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(phaze_analysis_audio_duration_seconds_total{job=~\"$job\", outcome=\"ok\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "audio-h / wall-h",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Audio-hours per wall-hour",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "The 1.4951x phaze-zaf2l measured at the production operating point (cap = 4 concurrent pods on the burst node). Note this counts one file's own wall clock, so it rises with concurrency by design -- phaze-8r6t4 priced W=4 at +83.6% per-file wall against W=2.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 4,
          "unit": ""
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(phaze_analysis_run_duration_seconds_sum{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])) / sum(rate(phaze_analysis_audio_duration_seconds_total{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "x duration",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Wall clock per second of audio",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "phaze-zaf2l measured 2.4480 files/hour over a 7-day window, and noted it is the LESS stable of the two throughput reads because it is blind to the mix of durations.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 4,
          "unit": ""
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(phaze_analysis_run_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\", outcome=\"ok\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 3600",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "files/h",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Files completed / hour",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Measured baseline: 4 hard failures against 4,383 completed analyses (0.0913%) at the time of phaze-zaf2l -- 3 AnalysisDecodeError, 1 AnalysisProbeError.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(phaze_analysis_run_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\", outcome=\"error\"}[$__rate_interval])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(phaze_analysis_run_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])), 1e-12)",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "failed",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Analysis failure share",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": ""
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(phaze_analysis_audio_duration_seconds_total{job=~\"$job\", outcome=\"ok\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "audio-h / wall-h",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(phaze_analysis_run_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\", outcome=\"ok\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 3600",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "files / h",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Throughput over time",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "id": 7,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Backlog -- a settled operator decision, not a fault",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "OPERATOR DECISION 2026-08-26, bead phaze-m1drf.5: asked how the 8,079-row awaiting backlog should be handled, the operator chose the option labelled 'Accept the drain rate' (durable record: repowise decision e1e3374e; the question as put is quoted in docs/telemetry/alerting.md). So backlog DEPTH is explicitly NOT a fault condition and nothing alerts on it. CAVEAT: these series are POLL-DRIVEN -- they are sampled by the admin UI's own /pipeline/stats read, so they go stale when no admin tab is open. Read them here; never alert on them.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 17
      },
      "id": 8,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (backlog) (phaze_pipeline_backlog{job=~\"$job\"})",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{backlog}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Files waiting, by stage",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "phaze-zaf2l computed 137.5 days (band 94-156) for 8,079 awaiting rows at 2.4480 files/hour. Informational: the drain rate is a settled decision, so a large number here is expected, not a fault.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 1,
          "unit": "d"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 17
      },
      "id": 9,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max(phaze_pipeline_backlog{job=~\"$job\", backlog=\"awaiting_cloud\"}) / clamp_min(sum(rate(phaze_analysis_run_duration_seconds_count{job=~\"$job\", outcome=\"ok\"}[$__rate_interval])) * 86400, 1e-12)",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "days",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Days to drain the awaiting queue at the current rate",
      "type": "stat"
    }
  ],
  "refresh": "30s",
  "schemaVersion": 41,
